---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title='Privacy Policy | Roadmap Labs'
  description='How Roadmap Labs collects, uses and protects your personal information, in line with the Australian Privacy Principles. We only collect what we need.'
  path="/privacy"
>
<article style="max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 96px 24px; box-sizing: border-box; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 26px">
  <header style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px">
    <span class="rl-tag">Legal</span>
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 60px); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.03em; font-weight: 600">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 30px; color: var(--text-secondary)">How we collect, use and look after your personal information. The short version: we only collect what we need, and we don't sell it.</p>
    <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; color: var(--text-secondary)">Last updated 8 November 2026</p>
  </header>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">Who we are</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">Roadmap Labs is an AI consultancy based in Melbourne, Victoria, working with businesses across Australia. In this policy, "we", "us" and "our" mean Roadmap Labs.</p>
      <p style="margin: 0">We handle personal information in line with the Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).</p>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">What we collect</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">We only collect what we need to reply to you and to work with you. That includes:</p>
      <ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 20px; display: grid; gap: 8px"><li><strong>What you send us.</strong> When you fill in our enquiry form or email us: your name, email address, phone number, business website and anything you choose to tell us about your business.</li><li><strong>Client information.</strong> If we work together, the business contact details and project information needed to deliver the work.</li><li><strong>Website usage.</strong> Like most websites, we may use cookies and analytics tools that record general information such as the pages you visit, your browser and roughly where you are. This doesn't identify you by name.</li></ul>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">How we use it</h2>
      <ul style="margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 20px; display: grid; gap: 8px"><li>To reply to your enquiry and organise your free session.</li><li>To provide, manage and invoice our services if you become a client.</li><li>To understand how people use our website, so we can improve it.</li><li>To send you occasional updates, but only if you've asked for them. You can unsubscribe at any time.</li><li>To meet our legal and tax obligations.</li></ul>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">We don't sell your information</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">We don't sell, rent or trade your personal information, and we don't share it with anyone for their own marketing.</p>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">Who we share it with</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">We use a small number of trusted service providers to run the business, and they may handle your information on our behalf. These include our form provider (Formspree), which delivers enquiries to our inbox, and our email, website hosting, accounting and analytics providers.</p>
      <p style="margin: 0">Some of these providers store data outside Australia, including in the United States. We choose providers with strong security and privacy practices, and we only share what they need to do their job.</p>
      <p style="margin: 0">We may also disclose information if the law requires it.</p>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">Cookies and advertising</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">Cookies are small files your browser stores to help a website work and to measure how it's used. You can block or delete them in your browser settings, though some parts of the site may not work as well.</p>
      <p style="margin: 0">We may advertise through Google Ads. If we do, Google may use cookies to show our ads to people who've visited our site, and to tell us how well those ads perform. We don't give Google your form details. You can manage how Google personalises ads at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">How we keep it safe</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">We take reasonable steps to protect your information from misuse, loss and unauthorised access. That includes using reputable providers, limiting who has access, and deleting information we no longer need.</p>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">Accessing or correcting your information</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it. Email <a href="mailto:dan@roadmaplabs.com.au">dan@roadmaplabs.com.au</a> and we'll respond within a reasonable time.</p>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">Questions and complaints</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">If you have a question about this policy, or you think we've mishandled your information, email <a href="mailto:dan@roadmaplabs.com.au">dan@roadmaplabs.com.au</a>. We'll look into it and get back to you.</p>
      <p style="margin: 0">If you're not happy with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px">
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; line-height: 32px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; font-weight: 600">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0">We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page, with the date it was last updated.</p>
    </section>
</article>
</Base>
